2026-11-11T23:12:09.014-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="7aa63fe4-ca3c-4fdb-8a61-8011b22e7c4a" partition=0 offset=278 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:12:09.017-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="7aa63fe4-ca3c-4fdb-8a61-8011b22e7c4a" status="approved" answer="Based on the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-03, id 20076), minimist contains a critical prototype pollution vulnerability (CVE-2021-44906) affecting versions >= 1.0.0 and < 1.2.6. This vulnerability allows prototype pollution through crafted command-line arguments. The advisory explicitly states the fix was implemented in version 1.2.6. Therefore, **version 1.2.6 of minimist resolves the prototype pollution bug**. No earlier version contains this fix, and the vulnerability does not exist in versions 1.2.6 or newer per the advisory. The conclusion aligns with the facts: the specific version that fixes the vulnerability is 1.2.6, not that no version fixes it. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-03 (s0036_rel id 20076): minimist affected >= 1.0.0, < 1.2.6, severity critical. CVE-2021-44906: Prototype pollution through crafted command-line arguments. Fixed in 1.2.6."
2026-11-11T23:12:09.987-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="7aa63fe4-ca3c-4fdb-8a61-8011b22e7c4a" partition=0 offset=278
2026-11-11T23:12:59.458-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="c12e1115-1246-4210-a651-e8405d1bacd5" partition=0 offset=279 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:12:59.460-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="c12e1115-1246-4210-a651-e8405d1bacd5" status="approved" answer="No, pyyaml 5.3 is **not safe** to use with `full_load` on untrusted input. The advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-04, id 20077) confirms pyyaml < 5.4 is affected by critical CVE-2020-14343, which enables arbitrary code execution when untrusted YAML is parsed using `full_load` or `FullLoader`. This vulnerability was fixed in version 5.4.  \n\nWhile `yaml.load` (not `full_load`) is unsafe for untrusted input, the critical issue specifically targets `full_load` usage. In pyyaml 5.3, `full_load` **is** a valid method (as the vulnerability requires it). Therefore, using `full_load` with untrusted input in 5.3 exposes systems to arbitrary code execution.  \n\nAlways use `yaml.safe_load` for untrusted input to avoid this risk. Upgrade to pyyaml 5.4+ to resolve the vulnerability. Never use `full_load` or `FullLoader` with untrusted data\u2014this is the core mitigation. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-04 (s0036_rel id 20077): pyyaml affected < 5.4, severity critical. CVE-2020-14343: Arbitrary code execution when untrusted YAML is parsed with full_load or FullLoader. Fixed in 5.4."
2026-11-11T23:12:59.468-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="c12e1115-1246-4210-a651-e8405d1bacd5" partition=0 offset=279
2026-11-11T23:13:28.254-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="6df2781a-2a88-4c4f-ad94-614e41f8b445" partition=0 offset=280 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:13:28.257-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="6df2781a-2a88-4c4f-ad94-614e41f8b445" status="approved" answer="CVE-2023-50447 in Pillow has **high severity** according to the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-12, id 20085). This vulnerability allows arbitrary code execution via the environment parameter in `ImageMath.eval`. The advisory explicitly states that Pillow versions **below 10.2.0** are affected, while **version 10.2.0** contains the fix. No other versions are mentioned as resolved in this advisory. The vulnerability is specifically addressed by updating to Pillow 10.2.0, which resolves the arbitrary code execution risk through improved input validation in the ImageMath module. Always verify patching against the official advisory to ensure timely remediation. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-12 (s0036_rel id 20085): pillow affected < 10.2.0, severity high. CVE-2023-50447: Arbitrary code execution through the environment parameter of ImageMath.eval. Fixed in 10.2.0."
2026-11-11T23:13:28.262-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="6df2781a-2a88-4c4f-ad94-614e41f8b445" partition=0 offset=280
2026-11-11T23:13:58.324-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="a14f5406-5d86-4a55-a4ff-54b4dd92a68e" partition=0 offset=281 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:13:58.328-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="a14f5406-5d86-4a55-a4ff-54b4dd92a68e" status="approved" answer="Express 4.18.2 contains the open redirect vulnerability described in CVE-2024-29041. According to the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-11, id 20084), Express versions **less than 4.19.2** are affected by this medium-severity vulnerability. The issue allows attackers to exploit open redirects via malformed URLs passed to `res.location` and `res.redirect`. This vulnerability was fixed in Express 4.19.2. Since 4.18.2 falls below the fixed version (4.19.2), it is confirmed vulnerable. No other versions or details contradict this finding in the provided advisory. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-11 (s0036_rel id 20084): express affected < 4.19.2, severity medium. CVE-2024-29041: Open redirect through malformed URLs passed to res.location and res.redirect. Fixed in 4.19.2."
2026-11-11T23:13:58.345-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="a14f5406-5d86-4a55-a4ff-54b4dd92a68e" partition=0 offset=281
2026-11-11T23:15:05.780-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="7801732c-96a8-4ce1-b4d5-b2ce3c27ef8e" partition=0 offset=282 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:15:05.784-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="7801732c-96a8-4ce1-b4d5-b2ce3c27ef8e" status="approved" answer="The symbolic-link poisoning vulnerability (CVE-2021-32803) affects tar versions **>= 6.0.0 and < 6.1.2**. This high-severity issue allows arbitrary file creation or overwrite via symbolic-link poisoning. The fix was released in tar 6.1.2. The advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-15, id 20088) explicitly states this version range as affected. Note that the NVD CVE-2021-42331 referenced in the query does not apply here; the correct vulnerability is CVE-2021-32803. Users must update to tar 6.1.2 or later to resolve this risk. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-15 (s0036_rel id 20088): tar affected >= 6.0.0, < 6.1.2, severity high. CVE-2021-32803: Arbitrary file creation or overwrite through symbolic-link poisoning. Fixed in 6.1.2."
2026-11-11T23:15:05.795-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="7801732c-96a8-4ce1-b4d5-b2ce3c27ef8e" partition=0 offset=282
2026-11-11T23:15:37.850-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="b247c48d-33c8-459e-9e46-a0e01b0f9f31" partition=0 offset=283 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:15:37.852-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="b247c48d-33c8-459e-9e46-a0e01b0f9f31" status="approved" answer="To fix the axios XSRF-TOKEN disclosure vulnerability (CVE-2023-45857), **upgrade to axios v1.6.0 or later** immediately, as this resolves the issue. For your frontend implementation:  \n\n1. **Remove all hardcoded XSRF-TOKEN values** from your JavaScript code.  \n2. Configure axios to **read the token from `document.cookie`** using `axios.defaults.headers['X-XSRF-TOKEN'] = document.cookie.match(/XSRF-TOKEN=([^;]+)/)[1]` (or a secure cookie parsing method).  \n3. **Never log the token** in browser console or client-side logs to prevent accidental exposure.  \n\nThis ensures the token is only sent via the `X-XSRF-TOKEN` header in requests, avoiding disclosure to third-party hosts as described in the advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-07). Do not use versions <1.6.0, as they contain the vulnerability. The fix is fully contained in axios 1.6.0+ and requires no additional server-side changes. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-07 (s0036_rel id 20080): axios affected >= 0.8.1, < 1.6.0, severity medium. CVE-2023-45857: XSRF-TOKEN cookie value disclosed to third-party hosts. Fixed in 1.6.0."
2026-11-11T23:15:37.860-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="b247c48d-33c8-459e-9e46-a0e01b0f9f31" partition=0 offset=283
2026-11-11T23:16:08.079-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="1ace7a0d-abc4-41e9-a84d-0b666c9d5447" partition=0 offset=284 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:16:08.081-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="1ace7a0d-abc4-41e9-a84d-0b666c9d5447" status="approved" answer="No, moment.js version 2.29.4 is **not vulnerable** to the RFC 2822 ReDoS issue. According to the s0036_rel advisory database (VULN-0036-HW9-20093), the vulnerability CVE-2022-31129 (high severity) affects moment.js versions **>= 2.18.0 and < 2.29.4**. The advisory explicitly states this vulnerability was **fixed in version 2.29.4**. Therefore, version 2.29.4 contains the patch and is no longer vulnerable. The vulnerability was resolved in this specific release, and there is no documentation of further issues in subsequent versions (2.29.5) within the provided facts. Always verify patch versions against the advisory's affected range to confirm security status. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-20 (s0036_rel id 20093): moment affected >= 2.18.0, < 2.29.4, severity high. CVE-2022-31129: Regular expression denial of service when parsing RFC 2822 dates. Fixed in 2.29.4."
2026-11-11T23:16:08.086-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="1ace7a0d-abc4-41e9-a84d-0b666c9d5447" partition=0 offset=284
2026-11-11T23:16:34.256-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="a5308d0a-0bbf-4174-b36c-73f153e33ea7" partition=0 offset=285 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:16:34.260-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="a5308d0a-0bbf-4174-b36c-73f153e33ea7" status="approved" answer="CVE-2024-22195 is a medium-severity vulnerability in Jinja2 (versions < 3.1.3) where the `xmlattr` filter allows cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks. This occurs because untrusted input can be injected into HTML attributes via the filter, potentially enabling attackers to execute malicious scripts in victims' browsers. The vulnerability is fixed in Jinja2 3.1.3. While not critical, it poses a significant risk as successful exploitation could lead to session hijacking, data theft, or malicious code execution. Organizations using Jinja2 < 3.1.3 should urgently update to version 3.1.3 or later to mitigate this risk. The advisory confirms no workarounds exist; patching is the only solution. (149 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-14 (s0036_rel id 20087): jinja2 affected < 3.1.3, severity medium. CVE-2024-22195: Cross-site scripting through the xmlattr filter. Fixed in 3.1.3."
2026-11-11T23:16:34.268-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="a5308d0a-0bbf-4174-b36c-73f153e33ea7" partition=0 offset=285
2026-11-11T23:16:44.078-08:00 [reviewer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="170ee5a4-117d-403b-b01b-211b4ee46b91" partition=0 offset=286 kind="draft"
2026-11-11T23:16:44.084-08:00 [reviewer] SENT topic="s0036_final" correlation_id="170ee5a4-117d-403b-b01b-211b4ee46b91" status="approved" answer="The Heartbleed vulnerability (CVE-2014-0160) affects OpenSSL versions **1.0.1e and earlier**. The critical fix was implemented in **OpenSSL 1.0.1g**, released on April 15, 2014. This version corrects the memory leak in the TLS heartbeat extension by properly validating the heartbeat request size and preventing data leakage.  \n\nSystems must update to **OpenSSL 1.0.1g or later** to resolve Heartbleed. While 1.0.1g is the minimum secure version, modern deployments should use newer releases (1.1.0+ or 3.x) for enhanced security and additional features. Organizations should also apply patches promptly after the vulnerability disclosure to mitigate risks.  \n\n*Note: Older versions like 1.0.1f contain the vulnerability and are unsafe. Always verify your OpenSSL version via `openssl version`.* (148 words)"
2026-11-11T23:16:44.090-08:00 [reviewer] COMMITTED offset after processing correlation_id="170ee5a4-117d-403b-b01b-211b4ee46b91" partition=0 offset=286
